cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "nmr-peak-assign: hypothesis-driven assignment of crude 1H NMR spectra using chemical-shift and integral cross-validation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shan
    given-names: Yingjie
    affiliation: "University of St Andrews"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-6218-1248"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24169336
version: 0.1.1
date-released: "2026-11-14"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/yingjieshanjrh-coder/nmr-peak-assign"
abstract: "peakassign sorts the peaks of a crude 1H NMR spectrum into product, unreacted starting material, solvent and unexplained signals. Candidate structures are supplied by the user; a peak is assigned only if both its chemical shift and its integral agree with a predicted signal, and significant signals that no candidate explains are reported."
keywords:
  - NMR
  - peak assignment
  - cheminformatics
  - reaction monitoring
